{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings","id":1492274,"title":"Arcana Interactions with other Supernatural beings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-04T02:55:38-07:00","id":1492274,"title":"Arcana Interactions with other Supernatural beings","content":"If I remember correctly, in 1st edition there was a sidebar that specified that since vampires are not technically alive any Life spell cast on them had to also include equal dots in matter to have effect. And in Mummy 2e it specifies that Mummies are inmune to spells that include Time or Fate. So I was wondering, are there any Arcana interactions with Supernatural beigns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T03:15:01-07:00","id":1492278,"title":"","content":"Players Guide to the Contagion Chronicles has the best resources for this. Specifically, the different Supernaturals have specific Arcana that can interact with their powers and themes. Changelings are mostly Mind and Fate, Werewolf is mostly Spirit, etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T03:19:56-07:00","id":1492279,"title":"","content":"I see, thank you! I don't have the Contagion Players Guide but I have been thinking about it fro a while. In retrospect I should have thought of the crossover manual from the start!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T03:22:17-07:00","id":1492280,"title":"","content":"Amusingly, the Mummy entry just says &quot;check Mummy 2e&quot;, so you're already on the right track","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T12:21:36-07:00","id":1492311,"title":"","content":"Mummies being immune to certain Time and Fate magic is a particularly exceptional element arising from their relationship with the Judges. Other supernatural beings don't have such patrons who make proprietary claims over aspects of their being.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure vampires mix Death with Life rather than Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T14:00:06-07:00","id":1492314,"title":"","content":"Sin-eaters are technically dead, but also walk around like living things. I think the use Death too. <br /> <br /> Demons are special and appear to be human, spoofing any powers with their cover. But the God machine is em... Prime and fate, i think.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are weird... Deviants are each unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T17:23:05-07:00","id":1492325,"title":"","content":"The most relevant bit from the CCPG is here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>A creature\u2019s basic nature doesn\u2019t change the Arcanum required to perform feats that normally fall under that Arcanum\u2019s purview except in specific circumstances.</b><br /> <br /> For instance, anything that\u2019s alive requires Life to affect in ways that would normally fall under Life\u2019s auspices, whether the subject is a Sleeper or a werewolf. The Arcana still individually apply based on what a spell does and how, as long as the subject is a valid one in the first place.<br /> <br /> The converse is also usually true: a mage doesn\u2019t need conjunctional Death to cast \u201cTelepathy\u201d on a ghost, because the ghost has a consciousness and therefore Mind alone works just fine. Some exceptions to this rule exist, and are listed under each game line below where applicable.<br /> <br /> If a subject isn\u2019t valid for a particular spell due to their nature, a mage may be able to affect them similarly with a different Arcanum if it makes sense given how the spell works. For instance, Life spells that physically manipulate a body don\u2019t work on vampires, because they\u2019re not alive; but since corpses fall under Death\u2019s purview, analogous Death spells can manipulate a vampire\u2019s dead body in much the same way. </div> </div> </div>By the same token, you don't need the Arcana for interfering with a monster's powers to affect the monster itself \u2014 Prime + Fate lets you meddle with Embeds and Aether, but Life is all you ought to need to turn a demon into a frog barring very particular circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T13:17:58-07:00","id":1492385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492280#post1492280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amusingly, the Mummy entry just says &quot;check Mummy 2e&quot;, so you're already on the right track</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read that section, and all it says is that Time and Fate magic, other than basic divinitory pratices. Has no affect on Mummies. That is certainl sigificant, but what magic does affect Mummies directly? <br /> <br /> Are they dead or alive or both for the purposes of the Arcana, or does it vary depending on their current state? <br /> Do they have souls that can be affected with awakened magic? (my guess here is &quot;Yes&quot; to souls, No to &quot;can be affected&quot; since it is likely that the Judges would have opinions on that as well)<br /> How does one dicker with Sekhem? I thought I had seen some of these touched on, but I can't remember where.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T13:34:58-07:00","id":1492387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492385#post1492385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just read that section, and all it says is that Time and Fate magic, other than basic divinitory pratices. Has no affect on Mummies. That is certainl sigificant, but what magic does affect Mummies directly?<br /> <br /> Are they dead or alive or both for the purposes of the Arcana, or does it vary depending on their current state?<br /> Do they have souls that can be affected with awakened magic? (my guess here is &quot;Yes&quot; to souls, No to &quot;can be affected&quot; since it is likely that the Judges would have opinions on that as well)<br /> How does one dicker with Sekhem? I thought I had seen some of these touched on, but I can't remember where.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, with very little knowledge of how Mummy works, I say;<br /> <br /> 1. Dead, so you need Death rather than Life to affect them for most things. Like a vampire.<br /> 2. They have souls, but the Judges have sufficient claim to stave off Awakened attempts at theft or major change. I think that was out-and-out stated somewhere in the Players Guide to the Contagion Chronicles book.<br /> 3. Not a clue. <i>Maybe</i> Prime, but from the sound of it it's on par with Primal Urge and Synergy, which can't be affected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-05-2022, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T13:52:35-07:00","id":1492392,"title":"","content":"I would say:<br /> <br /> 1- <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Arisen_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Alive if active, dead between Descents</a>. The Rite of Return allows them to achieve true resurrection and immortality, but in a quickly weakening state.<br /> 2- They need to have souls, their <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pillar_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Pillars </a>are based on the fivefold elements of the soul in Egyptian cosmology. Their souls can be affected, but are probably weirdly balanced or altered due to the Rite of Return, something that would make the mage have to pause and investigate what exactly they are looking at. The Judges would probably send other mummies to deal with soul thieves.<br /> 3- That is an easy one, Prime. In 1ed its stated <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sekhem_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Sekhem and mana are the same</a>. The difference is that, if you think about it as molten metal, Awakened magic manipulates it like a smith holding tongs, whereas Mummies do the spiritual equivalent of grabbing the molten ore with their bare hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-05-2022, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T14:04:06-07:00","id":1492393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492385#post1492385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they dead or alive or both for the purposes of the Arcana, or does it vary depending on their current state?</div> </div> </div> </div>They read as both to supernatural senses, so probably both Life and Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492392#post1492392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- They need to have souls, their <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pillar_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Pillars </a>are based on the fivefold elements of the soul in Egyptian cosmology. Their souls can be affected, but are probably weirdly balanced or altered due to the Rite of Return, something that would make the mage have to pause and investigate what exactly they are looking at. The Judges would probably send other mummies to deal with soul thieves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage's section on what can and can't have their souls stolen in Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed, where the Tremere get their 2e update, specifies that the Arisen can't have their souls stolen due to their being property of the Judges \u2014 that &quot;weirdly balanced&quot; aspect of their souls is the process of eternity-proofing them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is an easy one, Prime. In 1ed its stated <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sekhem_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Sekhem and mana are the same</a>. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454250#post1454250\">It says the opposite, man</a>.<br /> <br /> Sekhem is the stuff that Existence is made of. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454405#post1454405\">You can no more manipulate raw Sekhem with the Arcana than you can fabricate a completely new soul</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T14:22:34-07:00","id":1492395,"title":"","content":"I had not read the part about Sekhem in a while, fair enough.<br /> <br /> So they are largely immune to Fate and Time, their soul cannot be extracted. Which ultimately means their time limit cannot be artificially hastened and they cannot be permanently neutralized via Soulessness. Meaning an Obrimos and Mastigos would likely find the least anomalies with their magic if they run into a mummy for the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T14:59:54-07:00","id":1492398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492393#post1492393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sekhem is the stuff that Existence is made of</div> </div> </div> </div>I followed your links, and found out where that quote comes from, but I'm going to admit that I do not understand what it means.<br /> (thanks to everyone who answered)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T15:15:49-07:00","id":1492400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492398#post1492398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I followed your links, and found out where that quote comes from, but I'm going to admit that I do not understand what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sekhem is the metaphysical substance from which the Pillars of the Essence, Name, Spirit, Heart, and Shadow (i.e. the things Life, Matter, Forces, Time, Space, Mind, Spirit, Death, Prime, and Fate come from) are derived. Being able to grasp it in its undifferentiated form would require some sort of Reality Arcanum, which is basically what the Tremere have been eating souls for centuries in the pursuit of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T13:12:13-07:00","id":1492447,"title":"","content":"The Contagions Chronicles Players Guide (\u00a1Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> !) just points to Princes of the Conquered Land (Dark Eras Companion), which answers your questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492385#post1492385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they dead or alive or both for the purposes of the Arcana, or does it vary depending on their current state?</div> </div> </div> </div>They register as alive to Life sight and dead to Death sight. The book also states that Life spells can change a Mummie's body, so I would go on a limb and say that they are both for the purposes of awakanedmagic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492385#post1492385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they have souls that can be affected with awakened magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have answered, they have souls but are out of reach of awakened magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492385#post1492385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one dicker with Sekhem? I thought I had seen some of these touched on, but I can't remember where.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to PCl Mana is the light that shines upon the world while Sekhem<i> is</i> the world, the raw stuff of creation. Normally they don't interact but both Mages and mummies stretch this dualistic realtionship (Mages can alter the world without Sekhem, mumies can control Sekhem without Mana).<br /> <br /> Mages might not be able to control &quot;pure&quot; Sekhem but they can control Pillar points, kind of &quot;processed&quot; Sekhem that corresponds with one of the five parts of the human sould. Each Pillar corresponds with one of the subtler Arcana, Mages can sense Pillar points using Unveiling spells of the opportune Arcana and can seize Pillar poitns with a weaving spell, but can't store it inside her, so they must use an object as an artifical Vessel.<br /> <br /> Mages may use Sekhem as Yantras for spells of their associated Arcanum. The supplement also states that Mages might be able to do other feats with the raw stuff of existence, but only after &quot;deep research and stories of hard-won knoweledge&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T16:28:03-07:00","id":1492463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492447#post1492447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Contagions Chronicles Players Guide (\u00a1Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> !) just points to Princes of the Conquered Land (Dark Eras Companion), which answers your questions.<br /> &quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I had forgotten or never realized that the Dark Era's companion was an entity seperate from Dark Era's and Dark Era's 2, so I opted to buy it. Prince of the Conquered Land alone may have worth the price of the entire book. A lot of info.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T19:08:03-07:00","id":1492566,"title":"","content":"I'm also thinking right now about how, while Prime can't dispel things that aren't Supernal magic outright*, Clash of Wills is still a functional basis for what happens when a mage tries to cast a spell whose effect is contrary to the supernatural power employed by another being.<br /> <br /> And vice versa, so you could have an instance of something like a mage putting a Ban around a werewolf who gets a shot at breaking out using that one Gift that overcomes confinement.<br /> <br /> Although I do think there may be edge cases where it's a bit less certain what kind of power could be a counter. Like, say, that Theban Sorcery that causes a person to start vomiting beetles if they tell a lie, I'm not quite sure what you'd use to stop that from going into effect. <br /> <br /> * Although Fate actually does provide a means of breaking a limited range of supernatural powers regardless of where they come from, via indirect means (although not necessarily difficult ones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T20:04:44-07:00","id":1492567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492566#post1492566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I do think there may be edge cases where it's a bit less certain what kind of power could be a counter. Like, say, that Theban Sorcery that causes a person to start vomiting beetles if they tell a lie, I'm not quite sure what you'd use to stop that from going into effect. <br /> <br /> * Although Fate actually does provide a means of breaking a limited range of supernatural powers regardless of where they come from, via indirect means (although not necessarily difficult ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Thebian spell based on what the target <i>believes</i> is true? 'Cause you could hit them with a spell that causes them to believe their own lies for X turns every time they attempt to deceive someone. Not a Dispellation, but a neutralization","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T00:10:41-07:00","id":1492573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492566#post1492566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also thinking right now about how, while Prime can't dispel things that aren't Supernal magic outright*, Clash of Wills is still a functional basis for what happens when a mage tries to cast a spell whose effect is contrary to the supernatural power employed by another being.<br /> <br /> And vice versa, so you could have an instance of something like a mage putting a Ban around a werewolf who gets a shot at breaking out using that one Gift that overcomes confinement.<br /> <br /> Although I do think there may be edge cases where it's a bit less certain what kind of power could be a counter. Like, say, that Theban Sorcery that causes a person to start vomiting beetles if they tell a lie, I'm not quite sure what you'd use to stop that from going into effect. <br /> <br /> * Although Fate actually does provide a means of breaking a limited range of supernatural powers regardless of where they come from, via indirect means (although not necessarily difficult ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime is an odd one because it has Magic within its purview, and it is unclear if that means Supernal Magic only or all Magic. Like Supernal Vision and Prime Mage Armour bith work on generic supernatural phenomena (Supernal Vision with +1 reach), but word of Command needs additional Arcana to activate magic items.<br /> <br /> Supernal Veil can hide any Supernatural creature or active magical phenomenon from detection, but dispel magic is specifically Supernal Magic.<br /> <br /> I think with enough effort (scrutiny, preparation etc) a mage should be able to use Prime to suppress Theban Sorcery (possibly Prime weaving) or use Death's purview of endings to end the effect, or Time to fast forward the effect so long as it isn't indefinite. <br /> <br /> But to actually modify the effect might be subtler, is Theban Sorcery Death+Prime to alter (but not end)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T00:26:54-07:00","id":1492574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492566#post1492566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I do think there may be edge cases where it's a bit less certain what kind of power could be a counter. Like, say, that Theban Sorcery that causes a person to start vomiting beetles if they tell a lie, I'm not quite sure what you'd use to stop that from going into effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some sort of Prime shenanigans (an inverted Prime 2 Words of Truth?), or Fate 2 Fabricate Fortune ought to do it as I reckon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T00:39:29-07:00","id":1492575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492573#post1492573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime is an odd one because it has Magic within its purview, and it is unclear if that means Supernal Magic only or all Magic. Like Supernal Vision and Prime Mage Armour bith work on generic supernatural phenomena (Supernal Vision with +1 reach), but word of Command needs additional Arcana to activate magic items.<br /> <br /> Supernal Veil can hide any Supernatural creature or active magical phenomenon from detection, but dispel magic is specifically Supernal Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect 'passive' or 'reactive' manipulation of non-Supernal powers (protecting yourself from it, hiding from it, etc) is done by Prime alone, but 'active' or 'intrusive' manipulation of them requires Reach and/or other Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think with enough effort (scrutiny, preparation etc) a mage should be able to use Prime to suppress Theban Sorcery (possibly Prime weaving) or use Death's purview of endings to end the effect, or Time to fast forward the effect so long as it isn't indefinite.<br /> <br /> But to actually modify the effect might be subtler, is Theban Sorcery Death+Prime to alter (but not end)? </div> </div> </div>PGttCC says Space (not Prime, nor Death) cuts off any rites/miracles while they're being cast, since they're an esoteric usage of Blood Sympathy. So I suspect Space is what we need to 'hack' into rituals, maaaaybe with a Death requirement.<br /> <br /> However, it also says that defending against their end-effects is a matter of using the corresponding Arcanum, so say, countering Curse of Babel should require Mind or Prime, damage inflicted by Stigmata still requires Life to heal as usual, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T02:11:23-07:00","id":1492579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492567#post1492567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Is the Thebian spell based on what the target <i>believes</i> is true? 'Cause you could hit them with a spell that causes them to believe their own lies for X turns every time they attempt to deceive someone.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That could possibly work, although I don't think quite with the parameters you describe. Still, there are probably significant consequences to making somebody believe a lot of untrue things for a while.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492573#post1492573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime is an odd one because it has Magic within its purview, and it is unclear if that means Supernal Magic only or all Magic. Like Supernal Vision and Prime Mage Armour bith work on generic supernatural phenomena (Supernal Vision with +1 reach), but word of Command needs additional Arcana to activate magic items.<br /> <br /> Supernal Veil can hide any Supernatural creature or active magical phenomenon from detection, but dispel magic is specifically Supernal Magic.<br /> <br /> I think with enough effort (scrutiny, preparation etc) a mage should be able to use Prime to suppress Theban Sorcery (possibly Prime weaving) or use Death's purview of endings to end the effect, or Time to fast forward the effect so long as it isn't indefinite.<br /> <br /> But to actually modify the effect might be subtler, is Theban Sorcery Death+Prime to alter (but not end)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime covering anything not Supernal is highly exceptional. Mages can't even modify their own kind's spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492574#post1492574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some sort of Prime shenanigans (an inverted Prime 2 Words of Truth?), or Fate 2 Fabricate Fortune ought to do it as I reckon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really analogous to a conditional duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T02:29:09-07:00","id":1492580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492579#post1492579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not really analogous to a conditional duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was leaning (heavily) on the part where Vampire describes that specific ritual (and most ones, anyway) as a curse, and how Fabricate Fortune has &quot;falsify fates&quot; as its primary effect, for which &quot;trick Conditional Duration triggers&quot; is a mechanical example of what that could mean in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T04:14:50-07:00","id":1492585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492575#post1492575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PGttCC says Space (not Prime, nor Death) cuts off any rites/miracles while they're being cast, since they're an esoteric usage of Blood Sympathy. So I suspect Space is what we need to 'hack' into rituals, maaaaybe with a Death requirement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time they don't require conjunctional Arcana when possible. If you could borrow threads, or transfer the space effect, that would let you mess with them with Space alone (because if it is a sympathy think sympathic connections are entirely within the purview of Space). <br /> <br /> That said, there is more than one way to skin a cat, so i still think Time could wear out the effect so it ends as if it has run out of duration, or Death could weaving an ending to cause it to end prematurely (possibly requiring making if it has no ending to weave)... <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, it also says that defending against their end-effects is a matter of using the corresponding Arcanum, so say, countering Curse of Babel should require Mind or Prime, damage inflicted by Stigmata still requires Life to heal as usual, and so on. </div> </div> </div>Makes sense that life would heal, because you are just repairing a life pattern. Undoing end effects might be a clash of wills for some ongoing effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T04:24:48-07:00","id":1492586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1492274-arcana-interactions-with-other-supernatural-beings?p=1492579#post1492579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime covering anything not Supernal is highly exceptional. Mages can't even modify their own kind's spells</div> </div> </div> </div>Modifying a supernal spell is probably Archmastery, apart from during casting or Dispelling.<br /> <br /> But generally, Prime seems to be everything. Ephemeral Enchantment does more than death, mind, and spirit put together. Word of Unmaking affects all magic items (apart from Supernal artifcats) which given the context of Words of Command includes Werewolf Fetishes, Geist Mementos, and Changeling Tokens... <br /> <br /> Pretty much every example prime spell which is keyed to Magic (as opposed to Resonance or mana/Tass) includes all magical effects, except Dispel magic. So it seems quite the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}